==Scottish Gaelic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sga|gd}} {{term|benn||peak, point, pinnacle|lang=sga}}, from {{etyl|cel-pro|gd}} {{recons|benno-||peak, top|lang=cel-pro}}.

===Noun===
{{gd-noun|g=f|gen=beinne|pl=beanntan}}

# [[mountain]], [[hill]]
#: ''mar an ceò thall air a' '''bheinn''''' - as the distant mist on the hill
# [[pinnacle]]
# [[bin]]
# [[head]], [[top]], [[high]] [[place]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|mountain}} {{l/gd|sliabh}}, {{l/gd|monadh}}

====Derived terms====
